00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:50.000
God is telling you to say,

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.000
[39:11] ..."I have been commanded to worship GOD, devoting the religion absolutely to Him alone.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:01.000
So, there is no room for Jesus or Moses or Muhammad or the saints.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Huh? Yes.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:09.000
[39:12] "And I was commanded to be the utmost submitter."

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.000
The utmost submitter never complains.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.000
It's a sign of submitter or not.

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.000
The utmost submitter is content with whatever God gives him and understands.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.000
13,

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:31.000
[39:13] Say, "I fear, if I disobeyed my Lord, the retribution of a great day."

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:36.000
Submitters also realize that everything has a price.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:41.000
And this is now after passing all the tests. And you...

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:48.000
You've passed your final test. You're in good shape. And you cannot deviate outside

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:50.000
the path that God drew for you.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:55.000
Because if you deviate, it's very expensive.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:59.000
It seems out of proportion, but really it is not.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:07.000
You know, when I got pinched in the past, I'd say "No! This is too much! I didn't do that bad.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:08.000
And the answer would come back "yes."

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:14.000
This is it. You didn't do too bad, but this is the price for it. Yeah.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.000
The pinch is always way out of proportion, it seems.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:26.000
I guess because, you know, somehow we grew up with the notion that God is Forgiving, Merciful

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:30.000
which is true, but we tend to abuse this.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Son.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.000
God wants to make you perfect.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:46.000
And the system that I have noticed personally, and maybe you too, is that God will take one of

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.000
your defects at a time.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.000
And He will keep after you until you get rid of that defect.

00:02:56.000 --> 00:03:00.000
Then, He will start another one, until you cleanse out of that one.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:05.000
The end result is a perfect human being, if there is such a thing.

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:11.000
You'll be following God's commandments perfectly. And you'll be a perfect human being.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:20.000
So, the utmost submitter understands all these things.

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.000
Remember that the utmost submitter has a perfect life.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.000
The only reason you have a headache is because of something you have done.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.000
I don't think there are any exceptions to that. There are no exceptions.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.000
You don't get a scratch or a headache without something you have done.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:48.000
So, it behooves you to find out what it is that you have done.

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.000
Don't defend yourself either.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.000
I used to laugh when I tell some people "what did you do wrong?"

00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:59.000
"I didn't do anything wrong." You know, they become defensive.

00:03:59.000 --> 00:04:07.000
I say "hey, wait a minute, you're supposed to join me in attacking your "self" and find out what you did wrong."

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:10.000
They become very defensive.

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.000
But we're supposed to do this ourselves.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:16.000
We have to find out what did I do wrong.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:22.000
But if I, if I'm too egotistic to pinpoint what I did wrong, then I just go on.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:26.000
Because the punishment will continue until you know what it is.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:30.000
When you know what it is and you repent, it never happens again.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:32.000
The problem is solved.

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:40.000
So an utmost submitter means no problems of any kind.

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.000
It's almost unbelievable.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:52.000
But you see, God taught us repeatedly.

00:04:52.000 --> 00:04:55.000
God used me as a guinea pig, a happy guinea pig.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:05.000
I mean, I put myself in situations where a problem should have happened.

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:09.000
But it wasn't the cause of God, so a problem didn't happen.

00:05:10.000 --> 00:05:15.000
And the reason I'm saying this is because Ihsan is sitting here, and she expected a big problem.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.000
Thank you.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:26.000
I had... I was busy with this translation, and I slept here three nights in a row. I didn't go home for three days.

00:05:27.000 --> 00:05:32.000
And then, the answering machine... the telephone rang, the answering machine came on. My wife was on the phone.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:35.000
This is Stephanie. So, Ihsan started to run away.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:38.000
She said "this is it." She's gonna divorce you. You're finished.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:41.000
This is it. A big fight.

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:50.000
So, as she was approaching this door here to run away, she heard her say "I made a batch of Italian cookies, but they were so delicious.

00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:53.000
I'm sorry we finished all of them. So, I'm gonna make you another batch."

00:05:55.000 --> 00:05:56.000
She couldn't believe it.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.000
She, until now, she can't believe it.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:04.000
But this is... God manipulates the minds and the hearts of the people.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.000
In fact, this happened again when three or four weeks ago...

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.000
Huh? A few days ago when this visit.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.000
I slept here two nights in a row.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.000
And she called.

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.000
What did she say this time?

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:23.000
What did she want?

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.000
No, say it again. What did...

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:30.000
I want to chat.

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.000
I forget what she wanted, but it was peaceful. She was also running away.

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:37.000
Oh, yes, yes, yes.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.000
She said "I'm the happiest person in the world."

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:40.000
I said "what?"

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:42.000
Now, now I, I was insulted.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.000
"Ok. Wait a minute."

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.000
Honest, this is what she said. Yes, I remember now.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:51.000
She said "I'm the happiest person in the world."

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.000
I said "what's happened?"

00:06:52.000 --> 00:06:55.000
She said "I found the car I've been looking for, for a long time."

00:06:56.000 --> 00:06:59.000
"I'm like a baby. I'm like a child who found a toy."

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.000
This is exactly what she said.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:03.000
She's been looking for a car.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:13.000
So, I mean, this is a situation that warrants a problem, right, with most people.

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:15.000
"Where have you been?"

00:07:18.000 --> 00:07:19.000
"You're a half hour late."

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:27.000
"If you left your office at 2:30, you should have been here at 3 o'clock. It's 4 o'clock now."

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:36.000
